From b2107747d6a94cb3027d231f5b6da8a73822c75f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:55:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(brand): adopt the Hermes Studio girl icon and unblock
 CDN caching

Replace the Ekko Studio artwork with the hstudio-mobile girl icon and rename
the product surface to "Hermes Studio". Brand files keep stable filenames, so a
CDN edge kept serving the previous bytes for the whole max-age window and a
browser refresh never picked up a replaced icon; derive a content hash at build
time and append it as `?v=` so every release gets a fresh cache key.

- icons: logo, apple-touch-icon, favicon, icon-192/512/maskable, and the Hermes
  agent avatar (`coding-agents/hermes.png`) used left of the thinking indicator
- maskable art sits at 0.80 of the canvas (fuller desktop icon) on a background
  equal to `background_color`, so the WebAPK splash no longer shows a white plate
- titles: entry document, manifest, offline page, ChatView tab title, and the
  login heading in all 12 locales
- brand-asset-version plugin: rewrites the entry HTML plus manifest,
  logo-loading.css and offline.html; `deploymentUrl()` appends the hash at
  runtime. `sw.js` is excluded on purpose because its BRAND_PATHS set matches
  `url.pathname`, which never carries a query string
- pwa: bump CACHE_VERSION to v2 so clients drop the previously cached icons
- fix(mobile): keep the document in the browser scroll context so the native
  pull-to-refresh gesture reaches the viewport in a standalone PWA. `html, body`
  no longer pin `position: fixed` with vertical `overflow: hidden`; only the
  horizontal axis is clamped and `overscroll-behavior-y` stays `auto`. Height
  stability still comes from `--vh` (`1dvh`), which `.app-shell` consumes
