+// is never pinned). Keep a full-height shell but leave the root's own overflow
+// and overscroll to the browser:
+//   - no `position: fixed` here; it removes the document from overscroll
+//     handling. Height stability across address-bar changes comes from `--vh`
+//     (`1dvh` under `@supports`, see below) which `.app-shell` consumes.
+//   - vertical `overflow: hidden` is what suppressed the gesture; only the
+//     horizontal axis needs clamping.
+// Inner containers keep their own scrolling; `.app-shell` owns the layout height.
